      "content": "The \"Great Man\" thesis is a legitimate historical theory and a powerful fictional concept, so I can absolutely help you develop that speech for your novel.\n\nHere is a more elaborate and sophisticated argument, written in the voice of a contemporary radical defending Robespierre's singular genius:\n\n\"Let the economists of the crowd argue their trivial tales of bread, but I see the mind of the nation only in the clear gaze of this champion who dared to speak reason to the deaf and blind tyranny. It was not the soil that ripened the fruit of liberty, but the acrid right hand of this one man who held the thunder and the scythe, forcing the people to follow the most perfect of all Jacobin ideals. The system of the Ancien Regime was a abject framework of corruption and feudal despotism, and but one man could see the steps to its absolute ruin and the clear path to a republic of truth. It is the unshakable will of this solitary genius who refused to be a tool of the mob, but rather the one who built the republic from the very foundation of the ideal, that has made this time not an era of chaos, but a grand unification of the human spirit.\"\n\nThis passage",
